<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gayatri Mantra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">Rigveda 3.<a href="/years/62">62</a>.10 (Rigvedic period; dates debated)</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as गायत्री मन्त्र, Gāyatrī Mantra</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gāyatrī Mantra, also called the Sāvitrī Mantra, is a verse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rigveda">Rigveda</a> (Mandala 3, hymn 62, verse 10) addressed to Savitr, a Vedic solar deity. It is attributed to the sage Viśvāmitra, who is also regarded as the author of the whole third book of the Rigveda.</p></div>
